      "explanation": "Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.",
      "remediation": "Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.",
      "code_snippet": "| **megacave** | `/megacave` (alias `/caveman wenyan`) | Classical Chinese \u6587\u8a00\u6587. Far fewer characters, technical terms verbatim. |\n\nMode stick until changed or session end.\n`/caveman status` reports current mode without changing it. Claude Code and the standalone OpenCode plugin read stored state; other hosts answer from the conversation and mark it `(not tracked by this host)`.\n\n## Skills\n",
